+### `touchscreen-swipe`
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+Multi-finger swipe gestures on a touchscreen, replicating the touchpad behavior:
+- Vertical swipe to switch workspaces (continuous carousel).
+- Horizontal swipe to move the view.
+
+The gesture uses the same continuous animation and inertia as the touchpad swipe.
+
+On top of the animated swipes, discrete actions can be bound to taps and specific
+swipe shapes, and the horizontal swipe can be switched to resize the focused
+window. Anything left unbound falls back to the animated gesture (or, for taps
+with more fingers than `fingers`, to the regular `tap` action).
+
+The options are:
+
+- `fingers`: number of fingers required to trigger the gesture; must be 3 or 4
+  (default: 3).
+- `off`: disable touchscreen swipe gestures entirely.
+- `horizontal-swipe`: what a quick horizontal swipe does (default:
+  `"move-view"`). `"resize-column"` makes the swipe resize the focused
+  window's width, tracking the fingers 1:1: dragging right widens it, dragging
+  left narrows it, and the width stays where the fingers leave it. Tiled: the
+  focused column; floating: the focused window. Without a focused window the
+  swipe falls back to moving the view.
+- `tap`: action for a quick tap with `fingers` fingers (default:
+  `maximize-column`). All fingers down and up within a short window, without
+  enough movement to become a swipe.
+- `tap-more`: action for taps with one finger more than `fingers` (4 by
+  default); overrides `tap` for those.
+- `swipe-more-down` / `swipe-more-up`: discrete action for a quick vertical
+  swipe with one finger more than `fingers` (4 by default). Unset, such swipes
+  drive the workspace carousel.
+- `swipe-more-left` / `swipe-more-right`: discrete action for a quick horizontal
+  swipe with one finger more than `fingers` (4 by default). Unset, such swipes
+  keep the `horizontal-swipe` behavior (move the view, or resize the focused
+  column).
+- `hold { left/right/up/down { ... } }`: discrete actions for held swipes:
+  fingers resting still for a moment (~400ms) before swiping. A direction left
+  unset falls back to the animated swipe.
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    touchscreen-swipe {
+        // Example: horizontal swipes resize the focused window, a tap with
+        // one finger more opens the overview, an extra-finger flick down
+        // closes the window.
+        horizontal-swipe "resize-column"
+        tap-more { toggle-overview; }
+        swipe-more-down { close-window; }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    // Disable touchscreen swipe gestures.
+    touchscreen-swipe {
+        off
+    }
+}
+```
+
+### `touchscreen-edge-swipe`
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+Single-finger swipes that start at a screen edge: a finger starting within ~48 logical
+pixels of an edge and swiping inward past ~40 pixels (with the inward direction dominant)
+runs the action bound to that edge. Each of `bottom` (swipe up), `top` (swipe down),
+`left` (swipe right) and `right` (swipe left) takes any niri action.
+
+Touches in an edge strip deliver to applications normally until the trigger distance is
+crossed — plain taps and short drags on shell bars and app content keep working — and the
+compositor cancels the touch (and swallows the rest of the stroke) only when the gesture
+fires. A second finger landing cancels the gesture.
+
+The zones follow the output the touch lands on, including its transform, so edges stay in
+the visual orientation on rotated tablets and per-output on multi-monitor setups.
+
+Zones left unbound are inert. Avoid binding edges occupied by swipe-driven shell surfaces
+(e.g. a pull-down notification panel along the top): the bound gesture would fire mid-drag.
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    touchscreen-edge-swipe {
+        bottom { toggle-overview; }
+        top { spawn-sh "panel-toggle"; }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+### `touchscreen-corner-swipe`
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+Single-finger diagonal swipes that start at a screen corner: the corner zones are the
+~48 logical pixel squares where two edge strips meet. A swipe must move inward by ~20
+pixels on both axes — a mostly-straight swipe starting in a corner zone deliberately
+triggers nothing, so the adjacent edges stay usable right up to the corner.
+
+Corners win over edges when the touch starts within range of both. Each of `top-left`,
+`top-right`, `bottom-left` and `bottom-right` takes any niri action; unbound corners are
+inert.
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    touchscreen-corner-swipe {
+        top-left { focus-column-left; }
+        bottom-right { close-window; }
+    }
+}
+```
+
+### `debug-log`
+
+Log touchscreen gesture events for debugging: every finger down/up/motion with slot ids, positions and timestamps, gesture recognition (finger count, direction, hold vs quick), and the action dispatched for taps, discrete swipes and edge/corner swipes.
+
+The lines are prefixed `gesture-debug:` and written at info level, so they show up wherever niri's stderr goes (the journal for systemd sessions) without touching `RUST_LOG`. Off by default; the option can be toggled live, it takes effect on the next touch event.
+
+```kdl
+gestures {
+    debug-log
+}
+```
+
+To capture a reproduction:
+
+```bash
+journalctl --user -u niri.service --since -10m | grep gesture-debug
+```
