+### Touchscreen
+
+#### Workspace Switch
+
+Switch workspaces with three-finger vertical swipes on the touchscreen.
+The gesture uses the same continuous carousel animation as the touchpad.
+
+#### Horizontal View Movement
+
+Move the view horizontally with three-finger horizontal swipes on the touchscreen.
+
+#### Column Resize
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+With `touchscreen-swipe { horizontal-swipe "resize-column" }`, horizontal
+swipes resize the focused window's width instead of moving the view: the width
+tracks the fingers 1:1 while swiping and stays where they leave it.
+
+See [`touchscreen-swipe`](./Configuration:-Gestures.md#touchscreen-swipe).
+
+#### Edge Swipes
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+Single-finger swipes that start within ~48 logical pixels of a screen edge and move inward
+run a configurable action — for example opening the app launcher from the bottom edge.
+Each of the four edges binds its own action; touches deliver to applications normally
+until the gesture triggers.
+
+See [`touchscreen-edge-swipe`](./Configuration:-Gestures.md#touchscreen-edge-swipe).
+
+#### Corner Swipes
+
+<sup>Since: 26.04</sup>
+
+Single-finger diagonal swipes that start at a screen corner run a configurable action per
+corner. The swipe must move inward on both axes, so mostly-straight swipes near a corner
+stay with the adjacent edges (or nothing at all).
+
+See [`touchscreen-corner-swipe`](./Configuration:-Gestures.md#touchscreen-corner-swipe).
+
